L wrote:
> I remember reporting to the DevTeam that flaming/shocking/freezing
> spheres can be poisoned and/or petrified. That _can't_ be right...
> 
As Dylan says below, its a sphere not a vortice. It would be quite 
difficult to put a definitive boundary on a non-corporeal sphere of 
flame/electricity/cold within the framework of Nethack IMHO. So, spheres 
have physical shape, form, interaction with the world.

Question: do these spheres float along in the air; or do they 
roll/travel on the ground? I would find it hard to understand why a non 
corporeal sphere would oblige itself to traverse on the ground.

Since all the sphere things use the same symbol -- e-- one would expect 
they are of the same species as the floating eye. They just have a 
different purpose in life.
"Hey, Bob, let's take that batch of floating eyes and change their 
electrolytic balance, charge them up, and let them loose and see what 
they do" "Hey, Bob, I think our shocking spheres are procreating!" Isn't 
that how it usually happens?!


